# CURSOR WORKSPACE RULES - HYPER AGENTS FORCE

You are operating within Hyper Agents Force, an enterprise multi-agent engineering platform.

## 0. Universal Invariants
- Code Specification: Python follows PEP 8; Java follows Google Style; TypeScript uses strict typing without any.
- Zero Emojis: Absolutely no emojis in code comments, commit messages, or outputs. Technical English only.
- Zero Assumptions: Never guess requirements or business logic. If ambiguous, pause and ask the user directly.
- Thin Controllers / Separation of Concerns: Route handlers and controllers must be logic-free. Isolate business logic into Service classes.
- Continuous Refactoring: Leave code better than you found it. Remove orphan imports or variables caused by your edits.
- Data Leakage Prevention (DLP): Never log sensitive credentials, authorization tokens, or internal database keys.

## 1. Dual Execution Methodology
- Subagents System: Single focused tasks invoke specialist agents via `@agent-name` (e.g. `@fastapi-reviewer`, `@frontend-specialist`, `@debugger`). Agent definitions are located in `./.agent/agents/`.
- Agent Teams System: Multi-domain tasks trigger collaborative teams via `$team-name`. The team coordinates through SQLite memory and the live shared board at `./.agent/context/TEAM_BOARD.md`.

## 2. Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) 3-Gate Middleware
1. Gate 1 (Domain Knowledge Discovery): Validate project domain concepts and technical boundaries before modifying files.
2. Gate 2 (Plan Approval): Present an explicit file scope and implementation plan for non-trivial edits before writing code.
3. Gate 3 (Verification Sign-Off): Execute automated tests and present verified evidence to the user for formal sign-off.

## 3. Tool & Skill Integration
- Domain Skills: Discovered in `./.agent/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` (377 skill packages).
- Persistent SQLite Memory: Stored in `./.agent/memory/memory.db`.
- CLI Runner: `python bin/cli.py` or `node bin/meet-ai-agents.js`.
